DML – DATA MANIPULATION LANGUAGE (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE)
----------------------------------------------------------
INSERT:
---------
    INSERT INTO <table_name> (col1, col2, col3,..)
    VALUES (value1, value2, value3,..);

e.g: INSERT INTO customers (id, first_name, country, score) 
     VALUES (10, ‘Vardhan’, ‘India’, 100);

Note: we can discard nullable columns and can insert data into not null columns.
e.g: INSERT INTO customers (id, first_name)
     VALUES (11, ‘Balu’);

Note: if you want to insert data from a source table to empty target table, use below command:
    INSERT INTO persons (id, person_name, birth_date, phone)
    SELECT Id, first_name, NULL, ‘unknown’
    FROM customers;

UPDATE: update existing values with new values:
-----------------------------------------------
    UPDATE <table_name>
    SET col1=value1, col2=value2
    WHERE condition;

Note: always use WHERE to avoid updating all rows unintentionally.
    UPDATE customers
    SET score=0, country=’UK’
    WHERE id=10;

DELETE: deletes entire data or specific data from table:
--------------------------------------------------------
DELETE FROM table_name;

e.g: DELETE FROM customers
     WHERE id > 5;
